# Letters advance by their record's width byte when drawn.
name: 0190-letter-advance-draw
kind: module
module: 0
region: code
address: 0x306263c
gate: build refuses unless the stock bytes at the target equal
  `expect`. Pairs with 0191 and the letter tails in
  patches/antialias/font-glyphs.json and font-a-glyphs.json.
expect: 02a8
replace: 02e0
rationale: The glyph drawer (0x03062582) takes the advance from the
  record's tail byte, then, for A-Z and a-z only, replaces it with an
  ink measure (0x03063E06) of the top 10 rows (8 in the small font):
  leftmost plus rightmost inked column plus 2. Ink below those rows is
  not counted, so L, A and z could not be spaced correctly; the redrawn
  L sat 4 columns right of its slot ("F LAC"). This replaces
  `add r0, sp, #8` with a branch over the measure call and its `sxth
  r4, r0`, so letters keep the tail advance. Every A-Z and a-z record in
  both fonts is redrawn with a tail of width + 1, as every other
  redrawn glyph already has.
